---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import dataset from '../data/vulnerabilities.json';
const rows=dataset.items || [];
const pct = (x:number|null) => x === null || x === undefined ? 'Unknown' : (x*100).toFixed(2)+'%';
---
<Layout title="Vulnerability Intelligence | CyberIntel" description="CISA KEV, NVD CVSS and FIRST EPSS correlated with transparent remediation evidence.">
<div class="shell"><section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:16px"><span class="tag">VULNERABILITY RESEARCH / NVD + KEV + EPSS</span><h1>Prioritise with <span class="accent">evidence.</span></h1><p>Explore known exploited vulnerabilities with NVD severity context and EPSS probabilities. Priorities are descriptive, not proprietary scores or asset-specific findings.</p><p class="muted" style="font-size:13px">Snapshot: {dataset.updated_at || 'Not yet collected'} · Showing {rows.length} recently catalogued KEV entries · <a href="/methodology/">Methodology ↗</a></p></section>
<div class="stats" style="margin-bottom:22px"><div class="stat"><span class="eyebrow">KEV entries enriched</span><strong>{rows.length}</strong><small>Selected recent KEV subset</small></div><div class="stat"><span class="eyebrow">NVD responses</span><strong>{dataset.sources.nvd_success} / {dataset.sources.nvd_requested}</strong><small>Partial failures shown as unknown</small></div><div class="stat"><span class="eyebrow">EPSS</span><strong class="compact">{dataset.sources.epss_available ? 'Available' : 'Unavailable'}</strong><small>Probability, not confirmation of exploitation</small></div></div>
<div class="toolbar"><input id="vsearch" type="search" aria-label="Search CVEs" placeholder="Search CVE, vendor or product"/><select id="sort" aria-label="Sort vulnerabilities"><option value="recent">KEV recency</option><option value="epss">EPSS descending</option><option value="cvss">CVSS descending</option></select></div>
<section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><strong>Enriched vulnerability intelligence</strong><span class="muted" id="total">{rows.length} records</span></div><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>CVE</th><th>Product</th><th>CVSS</th><th>EPSS</th><th>Exploitation</th><th>Remediation</th></tr></thead><tbody id="vrows">{rows.map((r,i)=><tr data-search={`${r.id} ${r.title} ${r.vendor} ${r.product}`.toLowerCase()} data-epss={r.epss ?? -1} data-cvss={r.cvss ?? -1} data-index={i}><td><a class="accent" href={`/cve/${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}/`}>{r.id} ↗</a></td><td>{r.vendor}<br/><span class="muted">{r.product}</span></td><td>{r.cvss===null?'Unknown':r.cvss}</td><td>{pct(r.epss)}</td><td><span class="pill">KEV confirmed</span></td><td><a class="accent" href={`/cve/${encodeURIComponent(r.id)}/`}>View guidance ↗</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>{rows.length===0 && <div class="empty"><p>No data snapshot yet. Run <code>python scripts/fetch_vulns.py</code> after fetching CISA KEV.</p></div>}</section>
<section class="section"><div class="card"><h3>How to interpret this page</h3><p>A CVE in CISA KEV is known to have been exploited in the wild. It does not establish that any Shodan-indexed host, visitor or organisation is vulnerable. Version and configuration validation is required. EPSS estimates exploitation probability over 30 days, not CVSS severity.</p></div></section></div>
<script is:inline>
const search=document.getElementById('vsearch'), sort=document.getElementById('sort'), body=document.getElementById('vrows'), rows=[...body.querySelectorAll('tr')];
function update(){const q=search.value.trim().toLowerCase();let visible=0;const sorted=[...rows].sort((a,b)=>sort.value==='epss'?Number(b.dataset.epss)-Number(a.dataset.epss):sort.value==='cvss'?Number(b.dataset.cvss)-Number(a.dataset.cvss):Number(a.dataset.index)-Number(b.dataset.index));for(const row of sorted){const show=row.dataset.search.includes(q);row.hidden=!show;if(show)visible++;body.appendChild(row)}document.getElementById('total').textContent=visible+' matching records'}
search.addEventListener('input',update);sort.addEventListener('change',update);
</script>
</Layout>
